{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/910383-why-can-you-only-have-one-satiety-condition-at-a-time","id":910383,"title":"Why can you only have one Satiety condition at a time?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-08T16:07:50-07:00","id":910383,"title":"Why can you only have one Satiety condition at a time?","content":"Spun off from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast/page3\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> Losing Satiety and staying Slumbering aren't actually functionally mutually exclusive. But the Satiety section on Page 111 says you can only have one condition at a time.<br /> <br /> You could lose Satiety over time, but retain the Slumbering Condition...eventually you get to 0 and now gain the Ravenous Condition... which does 1 Lethal each day. If the Beast still refuses to wake the Horror (while starving to death from something decidely not what a human should die from), then the Horror wakes up after 10 days and feeds itself in the Primordial Dream. If the Beast manages to survive she has to deal with the fallout of trying to keep the Horror asleep.<br /> <br /> Aside from the RAW that you can only have one at a time, is there any other reasons for it? I rather like my idea and want to know what else is breaking from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T18:15:30-07:00","id":910451,"title":"","content":"Because the Horror is only Slumbering because it is full. If it is not full, it is hungry and awake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T20:52:45-07:00","id":910529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/910383-why-can-you-only-have-one-satiety-condition-at-a-time#post910383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Losing Satiety and staying Slumbering aren't actually functionally mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>The part of Slumbering that covers losing Satiety is specifically in the Resolution mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T08:12:09-07:00","id":910800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/910383-why-can-you-only-have-one-satiety-condition-at-a-time?p=910529#post910529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part of Slumbering that covers losing Satiety is specifically in the Resolution mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You lose Satiety as part of waking up, but just losing Satiety isn't listed as waking you up.<br /> <br /> To be clear, I like my idea, it requires a concious descion on the part of the Beast to risk and can have disastrous results (something I consider a good thing). I am not questioning the rules of the Condition itself, they are pretty clear. I am only asking about the WHY of the line on Page 111.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar414_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"414\" data-vbnamecard=\"414\">Gallus</a> That's a pretty basic way to take it and his fine. I just like the idea of Slumbering being a bit harder to get out of. And that the normal Satiety woulnd't do it alone. Unless there is a really good reason why not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T11:22:43-07:00","id":911779,"title":"","content":"EZ in what way is normal Slumbering easy to get out of?<br /> Option the first: Fill all your health boxes with lethal damage. IE you need to be put into a situation where you are on death's doorstep. Even if you arrange for that in a controlled environment you're still crippled for a while after your Horror wakes up unless you start burning through your remaining Satiety to fix yourself.<br /> <br /> Option the second: Collapse a chamber of your lair: If you're lair one this might be tricky, but doable. At higher lair ratings not so much and that's still not counting the fact that depending on the Beast the Lair might be a large number of horrific death traps and have a viable method of destroying it. Ie I don't think most STs will allow you to walk into a forest chamber punch a tree, make the check and destroy the chamber.<br /> <br /> Option the third: Make your way to the heart of your Lair and inflict at least three bashing on your Horror. Remember while your Horror is in a food coma you have none of the assets navigating your lair normally gets you, you can get lost in the maze, sliced by razors, drowned, incinerated, blinded, trapped in an inescapable room, and you have no easy way of navigating it. Remember just because your Lair might almost kill you in one of the chambers and trigger the first option doesn't mean your Horror would immediately merge with you and save you from the lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T11:41:03-07:00","id":911793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/910383-why-can-you-only-have-one-satiety-condition-at-a-time?p=911779#post911779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EZ in what way is normal Slumbering easy to get out of?<br /> Option the first: Fill all your health boxes with lethal damage. IE you need to be put into a situation where you are on death's doorstep. Even if you arrange for that in a controlled environment you're still crippled for a while after your Horror wakes up unless you start burning through your remaining Satiety to fix yourself.<br /> <br /> Option the second: Collapse a chamber of your lair: If you're lair one this might be tricky, but doable. At higher lair ratings not so much and that's still not counting the fact that depending on the Beast the Lair might be a large number of horrific death traps and have a viable method of destroying it. Ie I don't think most STs will allow you to walk into a forest chamber punch a tree, make the check and destroy the chamber.<br /> <br /> Option the third: Make your way to the heart of your Lair and inflict at least three bashing on your Horror. Remember while your Horror is in a food coma you have none of the assets navigating your lair normally gets you, you can get lost in the maze, sliced by razors, drowned, incinerated, blinded, trapped in an inescapable room, and you have no easy way of navigating it. Remember just because your Lair might almost kill you in one of the chambers and trigger the first option doesn't mean your Horror would immediately merge with you and save you from the lair.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> RAW, since you can only have 1 Satiety Condition at a time, and you automatically lose Satiety over time (nothing in the Slumbering condition says this stops), so you will automatically lose Slumbering when the timer expires on losing Satiety. Technically this isn't Resolving it so you wouldn't get a Beat for it though.<br /> <br /> I had proposed the situation in the OP before being pointed to the rule on pg 111 about only 1 condition being allowed at a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T12:02:19-07:00","id":911807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/910383-why-can-you-only-have-one-satiety-condition-at-a-time?p=911793#post911793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> RAW, since you can only have 1 Satiety Condition at a time, and you automatically lose Satiety over time (nothing in the Slumbering condition says this stops), so you will automatically lose Slumbering when the timer expires on losing Satiety.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Okay, I thought you were aware that you were proposing a hack beyond the matter of having multiple Satiety Conditions since you claimed to have read the relevant portions of the material, but:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slumbering, p321</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">She cannot spend Satiety for any reason <b>and does not naturally lose Satiety, no matter how many dots of Lair she has</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T13:36:19-07:00","id":911853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/910383-why-can-you-only-have-one-satiety-condition-at-a-time?p=911807#post911807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026Okay, I thought you were aware that you were proposing a hack beyond the matter of having multiple Satiety Conditions since you claimed to have read the relevant portions of the material, but:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh wow, I read that like 5 times and missed it. I feel dumb now. I still might think about the Hack (which it was, just one proposed with a mistaken premise) but I'll think about it some more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}